; Warnings, project-wide. The code already met this set before the stanza
; existed -- it is here so the compiler keeps it true rather than a reviewer
; having to. Warning 9 in particular (a record pattern that omits a field
; without saying `_`) is off by default and is what makes adding a field to
; a record a compile error at every site that should have handled it.
;
; 4 (fragile-match) is the one exclusion: it fires on every `_ ->` catch-all,
; which is why essentially nobody enables it. The rest of the default-off
; warnings here are off because they are about module-system style, not bugs.

